              "text": "Percent means per hundred. To express a share as a percentage, divide the part by the whole, then multiply by 100. The part and the whole must use the same units. A percentage describes a relationship; it does not tell you the size of the whole.",
              "figures": [
                {
                  "label": "The part",
                  "value": "6"
                },
                {
                  "label": "The whole",
                  "value": "24"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Share",
                  "value": "25%"
                }
              ],
              "chart": {
                "kind": "bars",
                "bars": [
                  {
                    "label": "The part",
                    "value": 6
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "The remainder",
                    "value": 18
                  }
                ]
              },
              "heading": "Understand",
              "kicker": "Out of a hundred",
              "delivery": "story",
              "break": "story"
            },
            {
              "text": "If 15 of 60 books are borrowed, the share borrowed is 15 ÷ 60 × 100 = 25%. That is the same share as 25 of 100 books.",
              "heading": "An example",
              "kicker": "Out of a hundred",
              "delivery": "story",
              "break": "story"
            },
            {
              "text": "Now, try this yourself. Choose a collection around you. Count a part and the whole, then work out the percentage.",
              "heading": "Try it",
              "kicker": "Out of a hundred",
              "delivery": "story",
              "break": "section"
            },
            {
              "text": "That's the end of Out of a hundred. Take a moment with the activity, then check your answer in the app. Thanks for learning with us.",
              "heading": "End of lesson",
              "kicker": "Percentages you can use",
              "delivery": "closing",
              "cue": "outro",
              "break": "section"
            }
